# Locale contributions

Authoritative guide: `pkgs/core/docs/i18nContributionGuide.md`. Prefer neighboring TypeScript locales as the live code pattern when the guide’s samples disagree.

## Adding or changing a locale

- Copy an existing locale (e.g. `en-US`) and replace values using [CLDR](https://www.unicode.org/cldr/) as the reference.
- Required pieces: `formatDistance`, `formatLong`, `formatRelative`, `localize`, `match`, and `options` (`weekStartsOn`, `firstWeekContainsDate`).
- Directory naming: usually `xx-YY`. Use the language-only code when language and country codes match, the language is used in only one country, or regional standards are shared across countries that use the language.
- Same-language locales: reuse `_lib` from the parent locale; override regional differences (often `formatLong` and `options`).
- Match patterns should be case-insensitive and cover diacritics / grammatical cases as needed; ordinals should match with and without suffixes.

## Snapshots

Always regenerate and verify:

```sh
mise //pkgs/core:gen/locales/snapshots
mise //pkgs/core:test/locales
```

## Docs lag (unclear / outdated)

The i18n guide still shows older JS/`default` export examples. Follow current TypeScript named exports in sibling locales (e.g. `export const enUS`). Do not invent a hybrid style.
